    "text": "Toourstockholders:\n2013 was a milestone year for Comstock as we were able toput in place all the ingredients to allow\nthe Company to be successfully balanced between oil and natural gas in 2014. Low natural gas\nprices, which continued through 2013,had weakened the Company's financial strength during a time\nwhen we needed to make investments in new acreage to grow our oil production. We made those\ninvestments and created a very successful drilling program in the EagleFord shale. Our investment\nin the emerging Wolfcamp shale play in West Texas did not create the successful drilling program we\nexpected but did provide the Company the opportunity to make a $230 million profit on its divestiture\nand repay $722 million in debt. The strong balance sheet created by this transaction allowed us to\nramp up our successful drilling program in our Eagleville field in South Texas and to invest in new\noil opportunities in the East Texas expansion of the Eagle Ford shale and in the emerging Tuscaloosa\nMarine shale. We are poised in 2014 to have a successful year driven by our oil production growth.\nWithnaturalgaspricesstarting toimprove in 2014,ourproperties inthe Haynesville andBossier\nshales in East Texas and North Louisiana provide us an opportunity to once again grow our natural\n2013FinancialResults\nWe generated a$41million, or85per share,profit in 2013.The profit was solely attributable\nNetIncome\nto the gain we recognized on the sale of our West Texas region. Oiland gas sales related to our\n$ in millions\n$41\ncontinuing operations increased 9% in 2013 as growth in our oil production and improved natural\ngas prices offset the decrease in our natural gas production. We generated operating cash flow from\nour continuing operations of $249 million in 2013 which was 7% higher than 2012's operating cash\nflow of $234 million. Our operating costs decreased 5% in 2013 to $85 million as compared to $89\n$(33)\nmillion in 2012. Lower transportation costs 